PN,37201
SC,0001
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F372A1786621677
OL,3,CLondon sets new record for A-level
OL,4,Cgrade gap over North East and East
OL,5,CMidlands
OL,7,FThe gap between the proportion of A-
OL,8,Flevel entries in London getting the
OL,9,Ftop grades and the equivalent figure
OL,10,Fin both north-east England and the
OL,11,FEast Midlands has reached a new record
OL,12,Fsize.
OL,14,FSome 32.7% of entries in the capital
OL,15,Fwere awarded A or A* this year, up
OL,16,Ffrom 32.1% in 2025 and the highest for
OL,17,Fany region in England, the exam
OL,18,Fresults show.
OL,20,FThe North East and the East Midlands
OL,21,Fhad the joint lowest rate, at 23.1%.
OL,1,W h7}h7}j7}h7}h7}                 G1/14
OL,2,W+,"-'*%/*-'"-'*%/T(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BLondon NewsCThis Day FReg TV
FL,373,370,120,260,000,100
PN,37202
SC,0002
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F372A1786621677
OL,3,CLondon sets new record for A-level
OL,4,Cgrade gap over North East and East
OL,5,CMidlands
OL,7,FThe gap between London and each of
OL,8,Fthese two regions now stands at 9.6
OL,9,Fpercentage points, the largest since
OL,10,Fthe present system of grading began in
OL,11,F2010, according to Press Association
OL,12,Fanalysis.
OL,14,FIn north-east England, the gap has
OL,15,Fwidened from 9.2 points in 2025,
OL,16,Fthough the proportion of entries
OL,17,Fgetting A or A* rose slightly this
OL,18,Fyear, from 22.9% to 23.1%.
OL,1,W h7}h7}j7}h7}h7}                 G2/14
OL,2,W+,"-'*%/*-'"-'*%/T(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BLondon NewsCThis Day FReg TV
FL,373,370,120,260,000,100
PN,37203
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F372A1786621677
OL,3,CLondon sets new record for A-level
OL,4,Cgrade gap over North East and East
OL,5,CMidlands
OL,7,FBy contrast, the East Midlands saw a
OL,8,Fdrop in entries awarded the top
OL,9,Fgrades, from 23.8% to 23.1%, the
OL,10,Fbiggest fall of any region.
OL,12,FThis pushed the gap with London up
OL,13,Ffrom 8.3 points in 2025 to 9.6 points
OL,14,Fthis year.
OL,16,FTwo other regions saw a year-on-year
OL,17,Ffall in entries awarded the top
OL,18,Fgrades: eastern England, down from
OL,19,F28.0% to 27.9%, and north-west
OL,20,FEngland, down from 26.6% to 26.5%.
OL,1,W h7}h7}j7}h7}h7}                 G3/14
OL,2,W+,"-'*%/*-'"-'*%/T(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BLondon NewsCThis Day FReg TV
FL,373,370,120,260,000,100
PN,37204
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F372A1786621677
OL,3,CLondon sets new record for A-level
OL,4,Cgrade gap over North East and East
OL,5,CMidlands
OL,7,FAfter London, the region with the
OL,8,Fhighest percentage of entries getting
OL,9,FA or A* was south-east England, at
OL,10,F31.5%.
OL,12,FThe results also show that for entries
OL,13,Freceiving the very top grade of A*,
OL,14,FLondon again has the highest figure
OL,15,Fthis year, at 12.0%, up from 11.6% in
OL,16,F2025.
OL,18,FNorth-east England and the East
OL,19,FMidlands have the joint lowest at 6.9%
OL,20,F` up from 6.8% in the North East, but
OL,21,Fdown from 7.4% in the East Midlands.
OL,1,W h7}h7}j7}h7}h7}                 G4/14
OL,2,W+,"-'*%/*-'"-'*%/T(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BLondon NewsCThis Day FReg TV
FL,373,370,120,260,000,100
PN,37205
SC,0005
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F372A1786621677
OL,3,CLondon sets new record for A-level
OL,4,Cgrade gap over North East and East
OL,5,CMidlands
OL,7,FThe East Midlands is the only region
OL,8,Fto see a year-on-year fall in entries
OL,9,Fgetting A*.
OL,11,FAt a national level, 10.7% of A-level
OL,12,Fentries this year in Wales received
OL,13,FA*, higher than the equivalent figure
OL,14,Ffor England (9.6%) and Northern
OL,15,FIreland (8.8%).
OL,17,FFor entries awarded A or above,
OL,18,FNorthern Ireland was ahead at 30.7%,
OL,19,Fabove Wales (29.6%) and England
OL,20,F(28.3%).
OL,1,W h7}h7}j7}h7}h7}                 G5/14
OL,2,W+,"-'*%/*-'"-'*%/T(,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
